/* This class illustrates how LAC context methods can be used.
LAC Context methods provide tools for creating XML nodes for report directly. They all have single common parameter LACContext - which is collection of report-related objects, and several handy methods
Best practice for context methods is to use ####_Extension class and add context methods there. You can have as many extension classes as you want. You can put all your extensions into single class, or separate them into several extension classes for better overview
Current class has name postfixed with _Tutorial not to interfere with standard extensions. Rename class replacing _Tutorial with _Extension, modify a few places where class name is used, compile module, and on LAC parameters click "Clear cache" to refresh extension methods cache */ public static class LACTutorialContextMethodsTutorial_Tutorial {
}

